Z||000000||Darren's 87 coupe||10-24-2001||10:05 AM||||i have a prestone flush and fill kit and it says to cut a hose and put in a tee to hook the water hose up to. Where is the hose I should tie into and do i then leave the tee installed in it forever? or do i then replace the hose?  Easy questions, but I have never done this and just want to know the best location for this tee.  <BR>Thanks <BR>Darren<P>ps, a pic would help, but not neded if you describe the location well enough<p>[This message has been edited by Darren's 87 coupe (edited 10-24-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000001||88CoupeV6||10-24-2001||10:29 AM||||It goes in the heater hose. In the front compartment near the firewall, almost under the windshield washer bottle. I don't cut the hose. I get a spare piece of hose and take the hose off the heater core and put the fitting on so I can take it back off after flushing so it will not look ugly in there. <P>------------------<BR>Josh<BR>   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/newsig.jpg">    <BR>:D  <BR><A HREF="http://albums.photopoint.com/j/AlbumList?u=1249362" TARGET=_blank>My pics</A>||||reg||7
Z||000002||K2m4||10-24-2001||11:34 AM||||Thats where mine is up front near the water bottle kind of by the passengerside going into the heater core. The guy who sold me the car was a FANATIC about flushing and filling his car on a regular basis. He said it works well ive never used it though.<BR>Kerm<BR>86 GT<BR>86 2M4<BR>88 2M4<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000003||Darren's 87 coupe||10-24-2001||11:51 AM||||Thanks josh, I think I'll try that route as well.  i wasn't looking to leave it in the whole time and that sounds like an easy way to do it.  Thanks<BR>Darren||||reg||1
